From 985f8de4220360649986d28d9643fc41c3c3aa34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 08:45:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 074/119] scene-referred S2 review fix: the light paths that
 bypass the BRDF helpers

Fable's S2 review rejected "area lights are 1.65 stops hot" as known breakage, correctly: the LTC
path never calling SpecularBRDF is a MISS of the pi unification (D4), not something D13 covers.
Fixed, together with the seven other bypasses the audit turned up.

Shader-only. No C++ changed, so no DLL was rebuilt or redeployed.

- Area lights, the required fix. AreaLightLTC_GGX now applies SCENE_BRDF_NORM_FACTOR to both
  outDiffuse and outSpecular, once, after the Fresnel/cosine term - so all six callers (Illum,
  Glass, HumanSkin, Terrain, MultiLayeredMaterials, and TiledShading's deferred
  LIGHT_TYPE_REGULAR_AREA branch) are covered by one multiply. The integrators return a bare form
  factor: LTC_Rectangle ends at `sum = len * scale`, LTC_Disk at `sum = formFactor * scale`, with
  no 1/PI anywhere, so this path carries exactly the same missing normalisation as DiffuseBRDF and
  SpecularBRDF.

- Seven more, found by the audit and fixed the same way:
  * ThinTranslucencyBRDF - the one that would have hurt most. It SUBSTITUTES for DiffuseBRDF in
    TiledShading's deferred translucent branch and in Vegetation's %GRASS / %LEAVES branch, so
    leaves would have been PI times brighter than the trunk of the same tree.
  * Hair (wrapped diffuse + two Kajiya-Kay lobes) and Eye (iris/sclera wrap + BlinnBRDF cornea) -
    own lobes, never touch the helpers.
  * Glass's diffuse wrap term only; its specular already goes through SpecularBRDF, and applying
    the factor to finalIlluminance would have squared it there.
  * The ocean sun glint (Water.cfx SunSpecular) and the particle sun specular (Particles.cfi) -
    ad-hoc lobes, but both driven by CV_SunColor, which is PI times larger on this path.
  * MobileComposition's two Lambert diffuse terms (not the desktop path; done for consistency).

- NOT given the factor, and the reason recorded for each: ambient lights (multiplicative tints),
  environment probes (a cosine-weighted cubemap is already E/PI and enters no BRDF), emissive,
  the sky family (emitters), decals (no light path of their own - deferred ones are lit through
  the G-buffer, forward ones are Illum's %DECAL permutation), SSS (a screen-space pass over the
  already-shaded buffer), and the bulb x121 round trip (unit-neutral, and folding PI in would
  desync culling radii from shading).

- The find of the pass: MultiLayeredMaterials' punctual BRDF is ALREADY fully normalised - its
  GGX NDF has `PI * sqr(denom)` and its diffuse is `diffuse / PI` - so it must not receive the
  constant. The corollary is that MLM has been PI times DARK relative to Illum on the STOCK path
  all along, and becomes consistent for the first time on the scene-referred one. Its area branch
  delegates to AreaLightLTC_GGX, so it was inconsistent with its own punctual branch too; that is
  now fixed as well.

Full classification of every light path - "gets the factor via X" / "does not need it because Y" /
"was missing" - appended and dated as scene-notes/research/s2-pi-and-light-units.md section 7.

Two things could not be settled by reading code, and are recorded rather than guessed: whether
LTCTex_2.w already carries the reference LTC's 1/(2PI) (this fix makes area lights agree with
point lights in the same engine, which is what D4 asks; the absolute calibration still needs the
section 6 experiment), and whether the ad-hoc lobes should be exactly 1/PI - they are tuned
approximations, so the factor is the defensible choice rather than a provable one, and their look
wants one eyeball pass against Illum.

Every change is one multiply by a constant that is exactly 1.0 off the switch, with no new shader
permutations.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01A72MFkdSczncE7au9UVnmu
---
 Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Eye.cfx            |  5 +++--
 Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Glass.cfx          |  4 +++-
 Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Hair.cfx           |  7 +++++--
 .../Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/MobileComposition.cfx |  5 +++--
 Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Particles.cfi      |  4 +++-
 Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Water.cfx          |  5 ++++-
 Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/shadeLib.cfi       | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 7 files changed, 35 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Eye.cfx b/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Eye.cfx
index 527a49e1..2d9320d1 100644
--- a/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Eye.cfx
+++ b/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Eye.cfx
@@ -317,8 +317,9 @@ void Callback_ShadingDirect(in ForwardShadingAttribs attribs, in ForwardLightPar
 	}
 #endif
 
-	diffuseAcc = cDiffuse.xyz * light.illuminance;
-	specularAcc = cSpecular.xyz * light.illuminance;
+	// D4: same as hair - the iris/sclera wrap diffuse and BlinnBRDF bypass the shared helpers.
+	diffuseAcc = cDiffuse.xyz * light.illuminance * SCENE_BRDF_NORM_FACTOR;
+	specularAcc = cSpecular.xyz * light.illuminance * SCENE_BRDF_NORM_FACTOR;
 }
 
 #include "ForwardShading.cfi"
diff --git a/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Glass.cfx b/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Glass.cfx
index 0cc0e347..ff7d9415 100644
--- a/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Glass.cfx
+++ b/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Glass.cfx
@@ -256,7 +256,9 @@ void Callback_ShadingDirect(in ForwardShadingAttribs attribs, in ForwardLightPar
 	else
     {
 		half3 finalIlluminance = NdotL * light.illuminance * NdotLBackLight;
-		diffuseAcc = finalIlluminance;
+		// D4: only the DIFFUSE term needs it here - the specular below goes through SpecularBRDF,
+		// which already carries the constant, and applying it to finalIlluminance would square it.
+		diffuseAcc = finalIlluminance * SCENE_BRDF_NORM_FACTOR;
 		specularAcc = SpecularBRDF(attribs.normal, -normalize(attribs.worldPos), light.lightVec, attribs.smoothness, attribs.reflectance) * finalIlluminance;
     }
 
diff --git a/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Hair.cfx b/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Hair.cfx
index f81b0690..c574ac4e 100644
--- a/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Hair.cfx
+++ b/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Hair.cfx
@@ -265,8 +265,11 @@ void Callback_ShadingDirect(in ForwardShadingAttribs attribs, in ForwardLightPar
 		cSpecular.xyz *= fOcclusion;
 	}
 
-	diffuseAcc.xyz = cDiffuse.xyz * light.illuminance;
-	specularAcc.xyz = cSpecular.xyz * light.illuminance;
+	// D4: hair uses its own lobes (wrapped diffuse, Kajiya-Kay anisotropic) and never calls
+	// DiffuseBRDF/SpecularBRDF, so it needs the normalisation constant applied by hand or hair is
+	// 1.65 stops hot against every other surface on the scene-referred path.
+	diffuseAcc.xyz = cDiffuse.xyz * light.illuminance * SCENE_BRDF_NORM_FACTOR;
+	specularAcc.xyz = cSpecular.xyz * light.illuminance * SCENE_BRDF_NORM_FACTOR;
 }
 
 #include "ForwardShading.cfi"
diff --git a/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/MobileComposition.cfx b/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/MobileComposition.cfx
index 24676659..ab498449 100644
--- a/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/MobileComposition.cfx
+++ b/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/MobileComposition.cfx
@@ -103,7 +103,8 @@ pixout LightingMobilePS(vtxOutWPOS IN)
 	// Sun
 	{
 		float NdotL = saturate(dot(attribs.NormalWorld, CV_SunLightDir.xyz));
-		diffuseAcc += NdotL * CV_SunColor.xyz;
+		// D4: bare Lambert, no 1/PI. The specular below is SpecularBRDF and already has it.
+		diffuseAcc += NdotL * CV_SunColor.xyz * SCENE_BRDF_NORM_FACTOR;
 		specularAcc += SpecularBRDF(attribs.NormalWorld, viewVec, CV_SunLightDir.xyz, attribs.Smoothness, attribs.Reflectance) * NdotL * CV_SunColor.xyz * CV_SunColor.w;
 	}
 	
@@ -146,7 +147,7 @@ pixout LightingMobilePS(vtxOutWPOS IN)
 			lightVec = normalize(lightVec);
 			float NdotL = saturate(dot(attribs.NormalWorld, lightVec));
 			
-			diffuseAcc += NdotL * illuminance;
+			diffuseAcc += NdotL * illuminance * SCENE_BRDF_NORM_FACTOR;  // D4, as above
 			specularAcc += SpecularBRDF(attribs.NormalWorld, viewVec, lightVec.xyz, attribs.Smoothness, attribs.Reflectance) * NdotL * illuminance * light.color.a;
 		}
 	}
diff --git a/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Particles.cfi b/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Particles.cfi
index 4b92ceaa..f92456ef 100644
--- a/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Particles.cfi
+++ b/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Particles.cfi
@@ -975,7 +975,9 @@ pixoutParticle ParticlePS(OutputVS IN)
 				sunIntensity *= IN.blendTC.w;
 			#endif
 
-			cSpecularAcc.rgb += BlinnBRDF(vNormal, vView, CV_SunLightDir, fGloss) * saturate(dot(vNormal, CV_SunLightDir.xyz)) * sunIntensity;
+			// D4: BlinnBRDF carries no 1/PI and sunIntensity is CV_SunColor, which is PI times
+			// larger on the scene-referred path.
+			cSpecularAcc.rgb += BlinnBRDF(vNormal, vView, CV_SunLightDir, fGloss) * saturate(dot(vNormal, CV_SunLightDir.xyz)) * sunIntensity * SCENE_BRDF_NORM_FACTOR;
 			cSpecularAcc *= MatSpecColor.rgb;
 
 			// combine with diffuse, but make sure we stay energy conservant
diff --git a/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Water.cfx b/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Water.cfx
index 3ead4247..3d4cf83d 100644
--- a/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Water.cfx
+++ b/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Water.cfx
@@ -986,7 +986,10 @@ void SunSpecular(in v2f_hs IN, half fNdotL, half3 vNormal, half3 vView, inout ha
 	// cSunSpecular *= saturate(dot(cSpecularAcc.xyz, 0.333)*dot(cSpecularAcc.xyz, 0.333)); // squashes sun specular result with low SunColor value
 
 	// Add sun specular term
-	cSpecularAcc.xyz += cSunSpecular.xyz;
+	// D4: an ad-hoc two-lobe glint, not a normalised BRDF, but it is driven by CV_SunColor - which
+	// is PI times larger on the scene-referred path - so without the constant the ocean's sun glint
+	// jumps 1.65 stops relative to every other specular in the frame.
+	cSpecularAcc.xyz += cSunSpecular.xyz * SCENE_BRDF_NORM_FACTOR;
 #endif
 }
 
diff --git a/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/shadeLib.cfi b/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/shadeLib.cfi
index 7734879d..2166aadb 100644
--- a/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/shadeLib.cfi
+++ b/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/shadeLib.cfi
@@ -822,6 +822,16 @@ void AreaLightLTC_GGX(float3 N, float3 V, float Gloss, float3 SpecCol, float3 po
 	// Apply fresnel and shadowing term + cosine factor
     float cosTheta_i = saturate(dot(center, N));
     outSpecular *= cosTheta_i * SpecCol * F_G.x + (1.0 - SpecCol) * F_G.y;
+
+    // SceneReferredSpec.md D4. The LTC integrators return a bare form factor - LTC_Rectangle ends
+    // at `sum = len * scale` and LTC_Disk at `sum = formFactor * scale`, with no 1/PI (and no
+    // 1/(2PI)) anywhere - so this path carries the same missing normalisation as DiffuseBRDF and
+    // SpecularBRDF and must receive the same constant, or area lights sit 1.65 stops above point
+    // lights on the scene-referred path. Applied once here, after the Fresnel/cosine term, so all
+    // six callers (Illum, Glass, HumanSkin, Terrain, MultiLayeredMaterials, TiledShading's
+    // deferred branch) are covered by one multiply. Exactly 1.0 off the switch.
+    outDiffuse  *= SCENE_BRDF_NORM_FACTOR;
+    outSpecular *= SCENE_BRDF_NORM_FACTOR;
 }
 
 // Diffuse BRDFs
@@ -894,7 +904,10 @@ half3 ThinTranslucencyBRDF(half3 N, half3 L, half3 transmittanceColor)
 	half transmittance = saturate((-NdotL + w) * wn);
 	half diffuse = saturate((NdotL + w) * wn);
 	
-	return transmittanceColor * transmittance + diffuse;
+	// D4: this SUBSTITUTES for DiffuseBRDF (TiledShading.cfi's deferred translucent branch,
+	// Vegetation's %GRASS / %LEAVES branch), so it has to be in the same convention or leaves are
+	// PI times brighter than the trunk of the same tree.
+	return (transmittanceColor * transmittance + diffuse) * SCENE_BRDF_NORM_FACTOR;
 }
 
 
